🐛 Describe the bug
Compiling models containing a while_loop HOP via inductor in an MPS device fails during code generation. The issue seems to rise from the kernel naming logic happening here, in the Scheduler for MPS via the Python path. The Scheduler is being instantiated more than once causing the counter to reset and therefore it generates kernels with the same name but different definitions.
Changing the Scheduler kernel counter to the C++ path's wrapper.next_kernel_suffix is a quick patch that unblocks the compilation. However, I'm not sure about the reasons of using self._kernel_fn_counter, probably @malfet can give more context. Bellow is one small repro and part of the generated error.
import torch
from torch._higher_order_ops.while_loop import while_loop

class CounterOnlyModule(torch.nn.Module):
    def forward(self, iterations):
        def body(i):
            return (i + 2,)
        def cond(i):
            return i < iterations

        (out_i,) = while_loop(
            cond,
            body,
            (torch.tensor(0, dtype=torch.int32, device=iterations.device),),
        )
        return out_i


if __name__ == "__main__":
    device = torch.device("mps" )
    iters = torch.tensor(4, dtype=torch.int32, device=device)

    model = CounterOnlyModule().to(device)
    compiled = torch.compile(model, backend="inductor")
    out = compiled(iters)
    print(out.detach().cpu().item())
torch._inductor.exc.InductorError: SyntaxError: failed to compile #include <c10/metal/utils.h>


    kernel void generated_kernel_0(
        device int* out_ptr0,
        uint xindex [[thread_position_in_grid]]
    ) {
        auto tmp0 = 0;
        out_ptr0[0] = static_cast<int>(tmp0);
    }




    kernel void generated_kernel_0(
        device bool* out_ptr0,
        constant int* in_ptr0,
        constant int* in_ptr1,
        uint xindex [[thread_position_in_grid]]
    ) {
        auto tmp0 = in_ptr0[0];
        auto tmp1 = in_ptr1[0];
        auto tmp2 = tmp0 < tmp1;
        out_ptr0[0] = static_cast<bool>(tmp2);
    }




    kernel void generated_kernel_0(
        device int* out_ptr0,
        constant int* in_ptr0,
        uint xindex [[thread_position_in_grid]]
    ) {
        auto tmp0 = in_ptr0[0];
        auto tmp1 = 2;
        auto tmp2 = tmp0 + tmp1;
        out_ptr0[0] = static_cast<int>(tmp2);
    }

 with program_source:592:17: error: definition with same mangled name 'generated_kernel_0' as another definition
    kernel void generated_kernel_0(
                ^
program_source:581:17: note: previous definition is here
    kernel void generated_kernel_0(
                ^

Versions
PyTorch version: 2.12.1
Is debug build: False
